        "applicationProcess": [
          {
            "mode": "Offline",
            "process": [
              {
                "children": [
                  {
                    "bold": true,
                    "text": "Procedure for Claiming Subsidy"
                  }
                ],
                "type": "block_quote"
              },
              {
                "children": [
                  {
                    "bold": true,
                    "text": "Step 1: Submission of Required Documents"
                  }
                ],
                "type": "paragraph"
              },
              {
                "children": [
                  {
                    "text": "The beneficiary/applicant submits the necessary documents in the "
                  },
                  {
                    "children": [
                      {
                        "text": "prescribed format"
                      }
                    ],
                    "link": "https://coffeeboard.gov.in/Schemes/ICDP_388.pdf",
                    "type": "link"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " after completing the relevant activity."
                  }
                ],
                "type": "paragraph"
              },
              {
                "children": [
                  {
                    "bold": true,
                    "text": "Step 2: Document Scrutiny and Field Inspection"
                  }
                ],
                "type": "paragraph"
              },
              {
                "children": [
                  {
                    "text": "The Extension Officer examines the submitted documents and conducts a field inspection. They forward the application, physical verification report, and all relevant documents to the concerned Joint Director (Extension) or Deputy Director (Extension), either recommending eligible subsidy release or rejection."
                  }
                ],
                "type": "paragraph"
              },
              {
                "children": [
                  {
                    "bold": true,
                    "text": "Step 3: Review and Recommendation by Joint Director / Deputy Director"
                  }
                ],
                "type": "paragraph"
              },
              {
                "children": [
                  {
                    "text": "The Joint Director (Extension) or Deputy Director (Extension) thoroughly scrutinizes the documents, ensuring the admissibility of the claim. They determine and approve the applicable subsidy."
                  }
                ],
                "type": "paragraph"
              },
              {
                "children": [
                  {
                    "bold": true,
                    "text": "Step 4: Release of Subsidy"
                  }
                ],
                "type": "paragraph"
              },
              {
                "children": [
                  {
                    "text": "Upon satisfying the claim's admissibility, the Joint Director (Extension) or Deputy Director (Extension) facilitates the release of the eligible subsidy to the beneficiary through Electronic Fund Transfer (EFT)."
                  }
                ],
                "type": "paragraph"
              }
            ],
            "process_md": "> **Procedure for Claiming Subsidy**\n\n**Step 1: Submission of Required Documents**\nThe beneficiary/applicant submits the necessary documents in the [prescribed format](https://coffeeboard.gov.in/Schemes/ICDP_388.pdf) after completing the relevant activity.\n**Step 2: Document Scrutiny and Field Inspection**\nThe Extension Officer examines the submitted documents and conducts a field inspection. They forward the application, physical verification report, and all relevant documents to the concerned Joint Director (Extension) or Deputy Director (Extension), either recommending eligible subsidy release or rejection.\n**Step 3: Review and Recommendation by Joint Director / Deputy Director**\nThe Joint Director (Extension) or Deputy Director (Extension) thoroughly scrutinizes the documents, ensuring the admissibility of the claim. They determine and approve the applicable subsidy.\n**Step 4: Release of Subsidy**\nUpon satisfying the claim&#39;s admissibility, the Joint Director (Extension) or Deputy Director (Extension) facilitates the release of the eligible subsidy to the beneficiary through Electronic Fund Transfer (EFT).\n"
          }
        ],
